<title>USA: U.S. Justice says GM Hughes units settle.</title>
<headline>U.S. Justice says GM Hughes units settle.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Justice Department said Thursday that two units of General Motors Corp's Hughes Electronics will pay $500,000 to settle allegations involving military contracts.</p>
<p>It said Hughes Aircraft Co and Hughes Aircraft Mississippi will settle allegations they did not properly test certain torpedo components as required under a U.S. Navy contract and used several non-conforming fasteners on several other military contracts.</p>
<p>The civil settlement resolved so-called whistleblower lawsuits filed in Mississippi by former Hughes employees. The Justice Department later joined the lawsuits.</p>
